## Project Summary

*AI-generated project summary produced by `/write-summary`, for future AI sessions catching up without re-analyzing line-by-line; may be out of date — re-run to refresh.*

### Purpose

Docker-based launcher for pre-made Claude Code agents. Each persona ships its own `CLAUDE.md` and (optionally) `.conf`; all share OAuth credentials, workspace mapping, slash commands, status line, skills, and toolchain caches. Multiple persistent sessions per agent; prior conversations resume automatically. Per-agent build *tags* and per-instance runtime *modes* compose into a layered Docker image and per-launch behavior.

### Tech Stack

- Python 3.10+ host launcher (walrus operator)
- `prompt_toolkit` (TUI picker), `python-dotenv` (`.conf` parsing), `rich` (markdown rendering for previews + F8 legend); stdlib `readline` for workspace tab-completion
- Docker + Compose v2; base is `debian:bookworm-slim` + Claude Code; `[prog]` adds Rust/Node/uv toolchains, `{auto}` adds iptables + sudo + firewall script, `{DooD}` mounts host docker socket
- No tests, no CI, no lockfile

